From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:51:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 80/85] web-app: match the audio download placeholder to the
 custom player
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The download-on-demand placeholder for audio/voice (desktop/0068) mimics
the native <audio controls> bar: a pill with a circular download button
where play sits, the duration, a fake track and the size. Since
desktop/0072 that is only half the story — with
experimentalAudioPlayerControls on, the downloaded message renders as the
custom player instead (full-width waveform on top, elapsed/total time and
a speed pill beneath), so the card visibly changed shape the moment the
download finished.

The placeholder now follows the setting: off, the pill stays exactly as
before; on, it renders the custom player's two-row layout with the
download circle in the play slot.

The layout classes come from AudioPlayer/styles.module.scss itself
(.customControls / .stack / .seekWrap / .metaRow / .time) rather than
being re-derived here, so the placeholder inherits the real geometry —
the 300px min-width floor and the min(70vw, 340px) phone override — and
cannot drift from it.

The one measurement that has to be restated is the waveform row's 32px.
.seekWrap is a column flex item with flex: 1, so flex-basis replaces its
`height` and the row is really sized by its content — the 32px range
input in the real player. The stand-in has to carry that height itself or
the row collapses and the time/size line rides up against the bar.

Two deliberate departures from the real player:

- The waveform is flat, and dotted rather than solid: a dashed hairline
  centred in the row reads as an inert stand-in, where a flat bar reads
  as a waveform that failed to load. It sits at 0.25 against the
  unplayed bars' 0.35, so "not downloaded yet" is legible without a
  label. There is no audio to analyse until the message is downloaded,
  and a canvas + worker round trip for a stand-in would be all cost and
  no information.
- The size takes the speed pill's slot. A speed control on a
  placeholder would be a button that cannot do anything — the same
  reasoning that keeps a play glyph off the video placeholder.

The elapsed/total pair is formatted with the player's own
formatAudioTime so both agree; duration is milliseconds on T.Message and
seconds in the player, hence the /1000. Senders that predate
Chat-Duration leave it at 0 and the total stays "-:--", as before.

Closes #160.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
